As part of the Telefilm Canada Feature Comedy Exchange, CFC hosted a special event on Monday, November 26 at TIFF Bell Lightbox: An Evening with Acclaimed Actress Leslie Mann and Comedy Powerhouse Judd Apatow. The evening was hosted by Richard Crouse, with an introduction by Eugene Levy.
Judd Apatow and Leslie Mann took the stage to discuss the ins and outs of making blockbuster hit comedies, working as a couple, and share their insights into the comedy filmmaking process. Director and star of the upcoming THIS IS 40, Apatow and Mann have worked together on many critically-acclaimed, box-office hits, including Knocked Up and The 40 Year-Old Virgin.
The Telefilm Canada Feature Comedy Exchange is a CFC North South Marketplace initiative in collaboration with Just for Laughs. 
Photo by Sonia Recchia.

To learn more about the Comedy Exchange, visit &lt;a href="http://cfccreates.com/comedy" rel="nofollow"&gt;cfccreates.com/comedy&lt;/a&gt;
